I have a complicated relationship with my mother.
label string3
Hate and fear has been cultivated in the society we grew up.
label string4
Just like I never truly know who I am.
label string5
I still remember the song she sang me to put me to sleep. I remember smiles, warmth, hugs. Sakha kisses when you kiss your relatives by smelling them
label string6
I don't know how much of all these complications is just life or colonialism. Or other structures.
label string7
I remember. So it means I resist
